# text = And it came to pass that after he had ascended into heaven-- the second time that he showed himself unto them, and had gone unto the Father, after having healed all their sick, and their lame, and opened the eyes of their blind and unstopped the ears of the deaf, and even had done all manner of cures among them, and raised a man from the dead, and had shown forth his power unto them, and had ascended unto the Father--
# sent_id = 817
# llm_note = AICTP frame; the 'that'-clause never resolves (fragment — the apodosis is cut off by em-dashes). 'after he had ascended into heaven' is advcl. 'the second time that he showed himself' is a parenthetical appositive inside the dashes. The long sequence 'after having healed...and raised...and had shown...and had ascended' are all advcl on the main (implied) action, coordinate under 'having healed'. Root = 'came' (main AICTP verb). The sentence ends with '--' (no full stop).
